research/audit/wave12-judge.jsonl-86-{"id":"rem-rn-conventions-and-scope","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"Section 1 says everything downstream of lem-metrics-on-rn inherits n >= 1, but immediately identifies downstream items such as def-euclidean-inner-product and p-norm clause 1 as valid at n = 0. The scope claim is self-contradictory.","context_sha256":"f79f27abf17fc3b511c1f6e6438fe580eeff53745dbd414fc6da42bcbf6c2380","item_sha256":"424ecf467fed615f7eadfec7388488d9c7b9c99744d0ac591e2e9f5913f0e494","at":"2026-08-10T03:52:06.770Z"}
research/audit/wave12-judge.jsonl-87-{"id":"def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":true,"reason":"Verified the componentwise derivative and integral constructions and their cited algebra, orientation, and subinterval consequences.","context_sha256":"c15b5fe92963f95f2c83952d1c586c9b51c1305f55ea5c0fa861b5247b9186d3","item_sha256":"ab91bc06583890723b84f2e2c05e1636a1ce3f8e57f88edacc60fb57390e233a","at":"2026-08-10T03:52:10.061Z"}
research/audit/wave12-judge.jsonl-88-{"id":"thm-norm-inequality-for-the-vector-valued-integral","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"Fact L10 asserts that a product of nonnegative reals is nonnegative, but neither cited lemma states that property. Thus L10 is stronger than its citations and does not faithfully supply the order fact used later.","context_sha256":"c25fa8643b7cebab766c3e761e49c0306509d75fcc0e66f0c1c24fffd15cff02","item_sha256":"441c9988e69f15648285dfde7cdca191c60b5688129340736b6cf562fb6febc7","at":"2026-08-10T03:52:15.125Z"}
research/audit/wave12-judge.jsonl-89-{"id":"fs-all-norms-on-any-real-vector-space-are-equivalent","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"Step 1.1 applies L4 to max of K and K prime, but L4 concerns finite sets of reals. K and K prime are von Neumann naturals, not reals, and no cited fact establishes their maximum or comparability, so the subspace closure step is unsupported.","context_sha256":"6c3a676ebe287b979a2ae40e551dd8cc6f6fa83ab73e0c9bed864b242c5abd94","item_sha256":"ef85605daf8363ac8ef1c5e6f1332c44969d19f7abd7ee53515483acc9e226eb","at":"2026-08-10T03:52:25.793Z"}
research/audit/wave12-judge.jsonl:90:{"id":"fs-heine-borel-holds-in-every-normed-space","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"L7 misstates its citation: lem-standard-basis-of-f-n defines e_i only for i<n in F^n, not the e_k in the infinite function space for arbitrary k. Thus its cited support for the pointwise description used in 1.1 and 1.2 is absent.","context_sha256":"7a179ac9354c8e557d875e7d2e75c07eee4841d6522c4c50a9d9c15b12eedaaf","item_sha256":"3081705d65baf819b9130a089349f1cad971c5944e48bbeed6868a0bf5e874d2","at":"2026-08-10T03:52:33.082Z"}
research/audit/wave12-judge.jsonl-91-{"id":"ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"Step 1.3 differentiates the scalar multiple t^(p+1)/iota(p+1), but L4 states only the derivative of a pure power. It cites neither derivative linearity nor the polynomial term-by-term conclusion needed to license that primitive.","context_sha256":"97e4e82d62dbf5888ec27763af531d363a289ca3839ea3f07cad4e1d696f35be","item_sha256":"ca465c9c3977d635e0e6424aebc9634bffd4c8a3ff8b2b88ece3c2d8c202a3f0","at":"2026-08-10T03:52:33.211Z"}
research/audit/wave12-judge.jsonl:92:{"id":"fs-heine-borel-holds-in-every-normed-space","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":true,"reason":"The counterexample (finitely supported sequences with N_infty, closed unit ball) is correctly proved to be closed, bounded, and not sequentially compact (hence not compact), with all steps properly citing valid dependencies.","context_sha256":"7a179ac9354c8e557d875e7d2e75c07eee4841d6522c4c50a9d9c15b12eedaaf","item_sha256":"3081705d65baf819b9130a089349f1cad971c5944e48bbeed6868a0bf5e874d2","at":"2026-08-10T03:54:04.323Z"}
research/audit/wave12-judge.jsonl-93-{"id":"thm-all-norms-on-rn-are-equivalent","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"Step 1.1 is not licensed by L6 and L9: neither states the real metric formula or the needed absolute-value facts. Thus r need not be established positive and the ball is not shown to omit 1, leaving closedness of S unproved.","context_sha256":"44852d7532f4b3947b26d888a05605585c4e3624077ad86ed1a24115f70ffbf9","item_sha256":"a6f99704289947e9d62b2ba4664a6509eeba214b19482d03c2b3e14e6927a64d","at":"2026-08-10T03:54:30.653Z"}
