research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/fs-heine-borel-holds-in-every-normed-space.md-3135-## Remarks
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/fs-heine-borel-holds-in-every-normed-space.md-3136-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/fs-heine-borel-holds-in-every-normed-space.md-3137-- **Nothing is claimed here about general infinite-dimensional normed spaces.** This library has not built that theory. What is exhibited is one real vector space carrying two inequivalent norms, which is all that is needed to refute the claim.
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/fs-heine-borel-holds-in-every-normed-space.md-3138-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/fs-heine-borel-holds-in-every-normed-space.md:3139:- **Where the proof of [[thm-all-norms-on-rn-are-equivalent]] breaks on $V$.** That proof takes the unit sphere of $\lVert\cdot\rVert_2$, which is closed and bounded, and concludes compactness from [[thm-heine-borel-rn]] — a theorem about $\mathbb{R}^{n}$ for a natural $n$, proved by bisecting finitely many coordinates. On $V$ there is no such theorem, and indeed [[fs-heine-borel-holds-in-every-normed-space]] refutes the corresponding claim on the same space.
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/fs-heine-borel-holds-in-every-normed-space.md-3140-
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/fs-heine-borel-holds-in-every-normed-space.md-3141-- **The two norms are the honest analogues of $\lVert\cdot\rVert_1$ and $\lVert\cdot\rVert_\infty$**, and the ratio $N_1/N_\infty$ at $u^{(m)}$ is exactly $\iota(m)$, the same constant that appears in the comparison chain of [[lem-every-norm-on-rn-is-continuous-for-the-euclidean-metric]] on $\mathbb{R}^{m}$. In finite dimensions that constant is a bound; on $V$ it grows without bound, and the Archimedean property is what turns that into a refutation.
research/audit/wave12-refuter-tasks/fs-heine-borel-holds-in-every-normed-space.md-3142-````
